adjudication.rationale:
In the diff, `Discourse.Group#findMembers` was changed from returning `Ember.RSVP.resolve([])` when `name` is empty to `return ;` (i.e., `undefined`):
```js
findMembers: function() {
  if (Em.isEmpty(this.get('name'))) { return ; }
  return Discourse.ajax(...)
}
```
So the method now returns `undefined` in one branch and a promise in the other. This is a real, verifiable inconsistency introduced by the diff, and any existing/other callers that do `findMembers().then(...)` (as was done previously in `afterModel`) would break when `name` is empty.

In app/assets/javascripts/discourse/models/group.js, addMembers returns the promise from Discourse.ajax(...).then(...), but inside the then-callback it calls self.findMembers() without returning it. That means the promise returned by addMembers resolves as soon as the PUT succeeds, not when the member list has actually been reloaded, and any rejection from findMembers() will not propagate to callers (effectively swallowed unless findMembers handles errors internally). This is directly verifiable in the diff:

```js
return Discourse.ajax(...).then(function() {
  // reload member list
  self.findMembers();
})
```

So the finding describes a real behavior/correctness issue introduced/present in the diff (same pattern also appears in removeMember).
